NNAAMMEE
       resizepart - tell the kernel about the new size of a partition

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       rreessiizzeeppaarrtt _d_e_v_i_c_e _p_a_r_t_i_t_i_o_n _l_e_n_g_t_h

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       rreessiizzeeppaarrtt tells the Linux kernel about the new size of the specified
       partition. The command is a simple wrapper around the "resize
       partition" ioctl.

       This command doesn’t manipulate partitions on a block device.

